    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear you on the \"openly acknowledging\" part, but honestly, I'm not sure I want to lead with it being a weakness. If we highlight it too much, the reviewers might just toss the whole thing before even looking at the results. \n\nIs there a way we could frame the n=12 not as a limitation, but as something more intentional? Like, can we present the data in a way that makes the small group seem like a strength or a specific choice for the study's depth?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
